  "question": {
    "text": "Two sides of a parallelogram are along the lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo></math> If the equation of one of the diagonals of the parallelogram is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then other diagonal passes through the point:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Lx08C",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OQShB",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iRIiW",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AGxNG",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
