  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Both the lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> pass through origin.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ffd4d3df-02f2-44e5-a72f-cec770588253-image.png\" style=\"width: 511px; height: 300px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;the point&nbsp;of intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>So upon solving we get the&nbsp;coordinates of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Also, point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is the point of intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>So, coordinates of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The diagonals of parallelogram bisect each other, so&nbsp;the mid point of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The equation of diagonal&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, the diagonal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
